WEBVTT

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:05.055
Poor detections create unnecessary workload and may erode trust in monitoring systems.

00:00:05.055 --> 00:00:08.895
If analysts repeatedly see alerts that are vague, irrelevant, or unactionable,

00:00:08.895 --> 00:00:10.255
they may learn to discount them.

00:00:10.255 --> 00:00:14.025
High-quality detections balance sensitivity with specificity.

00:00:14.025 --> 00:00:16.365
Sensitivity helps identify suspicious behavior,

00:00:16.365 --> 00:00:20.610
while specificity helps reduce unnecessary noise by focusing on events that match the

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.100
intended condition.

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.550
Detection engineers should consider whether alerts are understandable, actionable,

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.048
relevant, and maintainable.

00:00:27.048 --> 00:00:30.400
The output should explain what happened, why it matters, what entity was involved,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.560
and what context supports investigation.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.560
Reducing false positives improves analyst efficiency and supports better defensive

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.080
outcomes.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.720
The goal is not silent systems;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.560
the goal is a signal stream that earns trust because it helps people act with confidence.
